        "status": "success",
        "rationale": "The requirement has one behavioral obligation. For a requirement with `{sites}` or `{violations}` queries, the review prompt must direct the reviewer to apply the distributed-requirement guidance. `requirements.cli.distributed_guidance` is cited as context only, and its own tests are not reassessed here.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_review_prompt_applies_the_distributed_guidance]` is marked `{test}` for the subject. It loads the real bundled prompt through `review_prompt()`, which reads `habeas-requirements` `references/review-prompt.md`. It extracts the `## Criteria` section with `section()` and fails with `assert_text` unless that section contains the sentence \"for a requirement with `{sites}` or `{violations}` queries, apply the Do and Don't lists in the habeas skill's `references/distributed-requirements.md`\".\n\nThe asserted sentence carries the condition (`{sites}` or `{violations}` queries). It also carries the directive to apply the guidance, and it names the distributed-requirements reference that holds that guidance. `assert_text` uses `contains` and fails if the phrase is missing, so removing or weakening the directive would make the test fail. The prompt is static text with no further modes or branches, so no other scenario needs a test."
